diff --git a/docs/ops/logging.md b/docs/ops/logging.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e90c20b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/logging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+# Logging: archive, audit, alert
+
+PegaFila splits observability into three explicit lanes. Each has a purpose, a
+channel and rules of use. Pick one lane per message; never mix them.
+
+| Lane | Channel | Destination | Use for |
+| ---- | ------- | ----------- | ------- |
+| **Archive** | Monolog `daily` | `storage/logs/laravel.log` (14 days, `LOG_DAILY_DAYS`) | Routine application logs, `debug` to `error` |
+| **Audit**   | Monolog `audit` | `storage/logs/audit.log` (`info` min, 90 days) | "**Who** changed **what**" / "**who** tried **what**" events |
+| **Alert**   | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert` | Discord incoming webhook (`DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`) | Production incidents worth paging an operator |
+
+## Decision guide
+
+Ask, in order:
+
+1. **Is something actionable broken in production right now** (a job exhausted
+   its retries, a payment-gateway webhook is failing, a plan limit blocked an
+   entity)? → **Alert**: `DiscordOpsAlert::send()`.
+2. **Would an operator or auditor need to know who changed what, or who tried
+   something?** (membership role changes, subscription transitions, login
+   lockouts…) → **Audit**:
+   `Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [...])`.
+3. **Everything else** — debug traces, info breadcrumbs, per-request noise —
+   → **Archive**: `Log::debug/info/warning/error(...)` (goes to the default
+   `stack`, whose member is `daily`).
+
+### When *not* to alert
+
+- Pages only what a human can act on. Anything the code recovers from alone,
+  or that is only useful for post-mortems, belongs in **archive** or **audit**.
+- Discord is **not** a log channel. There is no `logging.channels.discord`
+  and none should be added: Discord alerts are an explicit call made by code
+  that decides an incident is worth waking someone up for, not a Monolog sink.
+- Do not alert from generic infra-wide places (exception handler, every
+  HTTP failure). Wire alerts where the actionable failure happens.
+
+## Alert: `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert`
+
+```php
+use App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert;
+
+// Resolve from the container; no constructor arguments.
+$alert ??= app(DiscordOpsAlert::class);
+
+$alert->send(
+    'Asaas webhook exhausted retries',   // title
+    'Payment intent #987 will not sync', // message
+    ['queue' => 'asaas-webhooks'],       // optional context
+);
+```
+
+Behavior contract (`app/Ops/DiscordOpsAlert.php`):
+
+- Reads the webhook URL from `services.discord.webhook_url`
+  (env `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`). **Not configured → silent no-op**, no HTTP
+  request.
+- Sends one `POST <webhook URL>` with JSON body `{"content": "<text>"}` via
+  Laravel's `Http` client, short timeout.
+- Text = title, message, then one `key=value` line per context entry
+  (nested arrays rendered as redacted JSON), truncated multibyte-safe to
+  **1800 chars** (Discord's limit is 2000).
+- **Redaction before sending:** keys matching `password`, `token`, `secret`,
+  `authorization`, `api_key`/`api-key`/`apikey`, `webhook` (case-insensitive,
+  substring match) redact their value; any string value containing
+  `Bearer <something>` is redacted regardless of key; nested arrays are
+  redacted recursively. Non-sensitive values stay readable.
+- **Soft-fail:** never throws. Non-2xx response or transport exception → one
+  `error`-grade archive log ("Discord ops alert failed"), with the webhook
+  URL (and everything else it embeds) scrubbed from exception messages.
+- No embeds, mentions, rate limiting or retries (out of scope on purpose).
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Env key | Default | Meaning |
+| ------- | ------- | ------- |
+| `LOG_CHANNEL` | `stack` | Default lane |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Members of the stack (default is **daily**, not single) |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Archive rotation |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Audit minimum level |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Audit rotation |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | *(unset)* | Alert webhook; unset = alerts off |
+
+## Rules
+
+- **Audit is for events, not noise.** One log entry per meaningful transition,
+  with ids in context (`subscription_id`, `user_id`, `from`, `to`).
+- **Never log secrets or PII** in any lane. The alert lane redacts
+  automatically, but do not rely on it: redact at the source.
+- **The webhook URL is itself a secret** (it embeds an upload token). Never
+  log it, and never commit a real one to `.env`.
